>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `FIRST_BEST_TAC`

``` hol4
classicalLib.FIRST_BEST_TAC : thm list -> tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Solves a goal by best-first search at the first applicable goal position.

`FIRST_BEST_TAC thms` first safely saturates the whole state. If no safe
step applies, it scans open goals from the left and expands the first one
to which an instantiating or unsafe fast step applies. This differs from
`BEST_TAC`, which then selects the first open goal. Frontier priority is
the total normalized syntactic size of all open goals. Children are
enumerated eagerly, without dynamic per-goal pruning.
`clasetSearch.node_limit` defaults to 100000 expanded states; a
non-positive value disables the limit.

The theorem list locally accepts `SIntro`, `Intro`, `SElim`, `Elim`,
`SDest`, `Dest` and `Del` markers. Unmarked theorems become unsafe
introduction rules. Generic simplifier markers such as `Cong`, `Excl` and
`SF` are ignored by the classical reasoner.

The tactic succeeds only when search and replay close every goal.

### Failure

Fails if no complete proof is found before frontier exhaustion or the node
limit. It can also fail while malformed extra rules are processed.

### Example

``` hol4
Theorem first_best_tac_example:
  (p /\ q) ==> (q /\ p)
Proof
  classicalLib.FIRST_BEST_TAC []
QED
```

